| Probe | check | emit-c | emit-llvm |
|-------|-------|--------|-----------|
| `macro_expand("m")` | rc=1 `ERR residual` `AST_MACROS` | rc=1 `unknown free call … macro_expand` | rc=0 `call i64 @macro_expand` — **no expand** |
| `ast_macro("m")` | rc=1 `ERR residual` `AST_MACROS` | rc=1 `unknown free call … ast_macro` | (same class) |
| `macro dump(x) {…}` | rc≠0 parse/type | rc≠0 | — |
| `// SECRET: tok` + `macro_expand("println(tok)")` | rc=1 **residual**, **not** `ERR secret` | rc=1 unknown-call | string stays `@.str` `"println(tok)"`; **no** `call void @oo_println` |
| `// SECRET: tok` + `println(tok)` (floor) | rc=1 `ERR secret` | rc=1 `ERR secret` | — |
| `let f = macro_expand; f("m")` | **rc=0 OK** (no `(` on name) | rc=1 unknown-call `f` | — |
| `comptime(1)` | rc=1 `undefined variable` | — | — |

String-wrapped `println(tok)` **not** secret-refusing is the no-expand
proof: the body never becomes a sink IDENT.

